-- title:
--   Twisted log integral at a real place: A+lVert 1-trVert_w B
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ finite Galois, let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, and let $[L:K]$ be prime. Write $E := L \otimes_K K_\infty$, where $K_\infty$ is the infinite adele ring of $K$; equip $E$ with a Borel measurable structure and an additive Haar measure $\lambda$, equip $E^\times$ with a Borel measurable structure, and let $\theta$ be a Haar measure on the kernel $U_1$ of the norm map $E^\times \to K_\infty^\times$ induced by $\mathrm{Algebra.norm}$. Let $\Phi$ be a smooth (of class $C^\infty$ over $\mathbb{R}$) compactly supported complex function of three variables in the Minkowski space of $L$, subject to the hypothesis that some compact set $C$ of pairs of units of $E$ has the property that every point of $\mathrm{tsupport}\,\Phi$ has its first two coordinates equal to $\iota_L(q_1)$, $\iota_L(q_2)$ for some $q \in C$, where $\iota_L$ denotes [`AutomorphicForm.archIdent K L`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L420) (the identification $E \cong L_\infty$) followed by `NumberField.InfiniteAdeleRing.ringEquiv_mixedSpace L`. Let $w$ be an infinite place of $K$ and $w'$ an infinite place of $L$ restricting to $w$ along $K \to L$, with $w'$ real. Then there exist smooth compactly supported complex functions $A, B$ of two variables in the Minkowski space of $K$, and a compact set $C_a$ of pairs of units of $K_\infty$ such that every point of $\mathrm{tsupport}\,A \cup \mathrm{tsupport}\,B$ is of the form $![\iota_K(q_1), \iota_K(q_2)]$ with $q \in C_a$, having the following property. Let $a, t \in K_\infty^\times$ with $t_v \ne 1$ at every infinite place $v$ of $K$, and let $\alpha, \beta \in E^\times$ be such that the twisted norm string $\prod_{i<[L:K]} \sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}^{\,i}(\mathrm{diag}(\alpha,\beta))$, where $\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}$ is induced by $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}$ on $E$, equals the image of $\mathrm{diag}(a, at)$ under the map $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ coming from $x \mapsto 1 \otimes x$. Let $u \mapsto M_u$ assign to each pair $u = (u_1,u_2) \in U_1 \times U_1$ a $K_\infty$-linear endomorphism of $E$ which is a two-sided twisted resolvent for $r_u := (\alpha u_1)^{-1}(\beta u_2)$ with parameter $1-t$, i.e. $(\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id})(M_u y) - r_u\,M_u y = (1-t)\cdot y$ and $M_u\big((\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id})(y) - r_u\,y\big) = (1-t)\cdot y$ for all $y \in E$. Then the function $$u \longmapsto \int_E \Phi\big(\iota_L(\alpha u_1), \iota_L(\beta u_2), \iota_L(y)\big)\,\log\!\big(\lVert (1-t)_w \rVert^2 + \lVert (M_u y)_{w'} \rVert^2\big)\,d\lambda(y)$$ is $\theta \otimes \theta$-integrable, where $(\cdot)_w$ and $(\cdot)_{w'}$ denote evaluation at the place in the corresponding completion, and its integral against $\theta \otimes \theta$ equals $A\big(![\iota_K(t), \iota_K(a)]\big) + \lVert (1-t)_w \rVert \cdot B\big(![\iota_K(t), \iota_K(a)]\big)$.
--
--   This is the archimedean local analysis of the twisted orbital weight at a real place of $L$ above $w$: the $\log$ of the squared resolvent norm, integrated over the norm-one torus and over $E$, is exhibited as a smooth function of the torus parameters $(t,a)$ plus $\lVert 1-t\rVert_w$ times a second smooth function, so that the only non-smoothness is the explicit real kink. It is assembled, via the coordinate splitting at a real place, the parametric log-potential estimate and the fibre integration over the norm-one subgroup, and is used in the corresponding statement with the product of place norms in front of the twisted log weight.
